It does vary by stage of the game.

Displacement costs 50, elven costs 60, so the DevTeam thinks
the elven cloak is better.  Much of that does seem to only apply
beyond the early game.

MC matters most in the midgame to a missile player if I think,
so I agree with you on that point.  A werefoo dead from vollies
of daggers and/or arrows is a werfoo that never gets to bite
you.

Elven cloak is magical so in polypiles it has a better chance
of giving other types of magical armor.  Polypiling is definitely
not an early game topic.

Elven cloak is elven armor so it can be enchanted higher than
other armor.  I can't recall ever trying to max out an elven cloak
this way as by the time I have enough ?oEA I usually have a
robe or [oMR instead.  So to me that's only a difference that
would apply in an extinctionist or pudding farming game.

Displacement works on nearly all monsters in the early levels
and on fewer and fewer as you go deeper.  Compare with stealth.
Stealth works by your sound not reaching distant monsters so
they can't zero in on you easily.  It also means you do not wake
up sleeping monsters by walking around or even with combat.
This makes clearing out a barracks or leprechaun hall a matter
of killing them one by one in their spot.

To me the biggest difference with and without stealth is nymphs -
Stealth reduces the problem of waking nymphs.  Without stealth
my characters are often surprised by advancing nymphs.  With
stealth my characters usually encounter sleeping nymphs so I
get to avoid them or get in the first hit.  Shooting volleys of arrows
and/or daggers starting at maximum range, and nymphs usually
become a source of items.

I have enough problems wwith nymphs that I value stealth over
displacement in the early game, but let's think about this in
terms of a ranger.  A ranger is supposed to be a distance fighter
who avoids getting into melee.  For a ranger, being able to strike
silently at range should outrank being elusive once you can no
longer avoid being face to face.

The more I think about this the more I'd want stealth over
displacement.  And since stealth comes from elven cloak and/or
elven boots it becomes a choice among more types of armor
than just cloaks.  Give me elven boots and then I won't mind
a cloak of displacement over elven cloak.  Until elven boots
arrive, I would remain tempted to put a [oD into my bag in
favor of elven cloak.



